        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "20849449"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Involved in the degradation of ectoine, which allows H.elongata to utilize ectoine as both a carbon and a nitrogen source for growth. Probably catalyzes the conversion of L-2,4-diaminobutyrate (DABA) to L-aspartate beta-semialdehyde (ASA) by transamination with 2-oxoglutarate"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
    {
      "commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY",
      "reaction": {
        "name": "L-2,4-diaminobutanoate + 2-oxoglutarate = L-aspartate 4-semialdehyde + L-glutamate",
