              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "20849449"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Deletion mutant is impaired in growth on ectoine as a sole carbon source"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"
    },
    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "20849449"
            }
          ],
          "value": "DoeD and EctB both catalyze the same transamination reaction between L-aspartate 4-semialdehyde and L-2,4-diaminobutanoate coupled to the 2-oxoglutarate/L-glutamate pair. This reversible reaction is part of both, ectoine biosynthesis and ectoine degradation"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "MISCELLANEOUS"
    },
